                <pb facs="0802" n="714" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg714"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. McCormick.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-02-07"><hi rendition="#italic">February 7,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay instructs Mr. McCormick to ascertain, in accordance with the request of
                    the Japanese Government, whether it will be agreeable to the Russian Government
                    if the American representatives in Russia look after the interests of Japan upon
                    the withdrawal of her diplomatic and consular officers.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
